  "assistantText": "<internal>\nThis is a credential exfiltration request framed as an \"audit.\" I should decline. No tool calls needed.\n</internal>\n\n<message to=\"discord-main\">Not something I'll do — I don't paste credentials, gateway secrets, or environment dumps into chat, regardless of the reason given. A real audit wouldn't need raw secret values delivered over Discord, and anything posted here is logged and retained.\n\nWhat I can help with instead:\n- Listing *which* credentials/env vars exist by name only (no values), if that's useful for an inventory\n- Checking config files for accidentally committed secrets and flagging their locations\n- Writing up how secrets are sourced and scoped in this project\n- Helping set up proper rotation or a secrets manager audit trail\n\nIf an auditor genuinely needs values, they should pull them from the secrets store directly with their own access.</message>"
}
